🧠 5. Fragmentation
❓ Question
What is memory fragmentation? How does it affect performance?
✅ Strong Answer
🔹 Types
Internal Fragmentation
Allocated memory > required
External Fragmentation
Free memory exists but not contiguous
🔹 Impact
Allocation failures
Increased latency
Cache inefficiency
🔹 Example

[Free][Used][Free][Used][Free]

→ Cannot allocate large contiguous block
🔥 Staff-Level Insight
“Fragmentation becomes critical in long-running systems like servers or embedded systems where uptime is high.”
❓ Follow-up
Q: How to reduce fragmentation?
✅ Answer
Memory pools
Custom allocators
Object reuse
Slab allocation

❓ Deep Question
Why is fragmentation worse in heap but not stack?
👉 Stack is LIFO → no holes
👉 Heap is arbitrary → holes form
🚀 Final Staff-Level Tip
When answering, always:
1. Start simple
2. Add trade-offs
3. Add real-world insight

🎯 Example Closing Line (Impressive)
“In production systems, especially embedded or high-throughput services, I carefully control heap usage, prefer RAII-based designs,
and avoid shared ownership unless absolutely necessary to reduce fragmentation and contention.”

