🧠 2. Design a Rate Limiter (Amazon/Google common)
❓ Question
Design a distributed rate limiter. Also implement a thread-safe in-memory limiter in C++.
✅ Answer
🔹 System Design
Use:
Token bucket / leaky bucket
Distributed:
Redis / centralized store
Consistent hashing
🔹 Trade-offs
Strong consistency → slower
Eventual consistency → faster but approximate
🔹 C++ Implementation (Thread-safe)
class RateLimiter {
    int tokens;
    std::mutex m;

public:
    bool allow() {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m);
        if (tokens > 0) {
            tokens--;
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
};

🔹 Optimization (Staff-Level)
Use lock-free structures or atomic counters
Reduce contention via sharding
🔥 Staff Insight
“At high QPS, a single mutex becomes a bottleneck, so I’d shard the limiter across cores.”
🔥 What they test
Concurrency + scalability thinking
